.TE
.PP
When in doubt, add parentheses: they cost nothing.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
void main() {
    i64 a = 2, b = 3, c = 4;
    printf("%d %d\en", a + b * c, (a + b) * c);
    printf("%d %d\en", 1 << 2 + 1, (1 << 2) + 1);
    printf("%d %d\en", 6 & 3 == 3, (6 & 3) == 2);
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Output:
.RS 4
.EX
14 20
8 5
0 1
.EE
.RE
.PP
The middle line shows a classic trap: \fB+\fR binds tighter than \fB<<\fR\&. So does the last one: \fB==\fR binds tighter than \fB&\fR\&.
